\c 2
\s1 Israel Rebuked at Bochim
\p \v 1 \w Now the angel|strong="H4397"\w*\f + \fr 2:1 \ft Or \fqa Angel\ft ; also in verse 4\f* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w went up|strong="H5927"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w Gilgal|strong="H1537"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Bochim|strong="H1066"\w* \w and said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w I brought you up|strong="H5927"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w out of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w* \w and led|strong="H935"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w you into|strong="H413"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w I had promised|strong="H7650"\w* \w to your fathers|strong="H1"\w*, \w and I said|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w I will never|strong="H3808"\w* \w . . .|strong="H5769"\w* \w break|strong="H6565"\w* \w My covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w with you|strong="H854"\w*, \v 2 \w and you|strong="H859"\w* \w are not|strong="H3808"\w* \w to make|strong="H3772"\w* \w a covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w with the people|strong="H3427"\w* \w of this|strong="H2063"\w* \w land|strong="H776"\w*, \w but you shall tear down|strong="H5422"\w* \w their altars|strong="H4196"\w*.’
