\c 7
\s1 Gideon’s Army of Three Hundred
\p \v 1 \w Early in the morning|strong="H7925"\w* \w Jerubbaal|strong="H3378"\w*\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa Jerubbaal \ft is another name for \fqa Gideon \ft and probably means \fqa let Baal contend\ft ; see \ref Judges 6:32|JDG 6:32\ref*.\f* \w (that is|strong="H1931"\w*, \w Gideon|strong="H1439"\w*) \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the men|strong="H5971"\w* \w -|strong="H834"\w* \w with him|strong="H854"\w* \w camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w beside|strong="H5921"\w* \w vvv|strong="H5878"\w* \w the spring of Harod|strong="H5878"\w*. \w And the camp|strong="H4264"\w* \w of Midian|strong="H4080"\w* \w was|strong="H1961"\w* \w north|strong="H6828"\w* of them \w in the valley|strong="H6010"\w* \w near the hill|strong="H1389"\w* \w of Moreh|strong="H4176"\w*.
