\p \v 27 \w [From all this] Gideon|strong="H1439"\w* \w made|strong="H6213"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w an ephod|strong="H646"\w*, \w which he placed|strong="H3322"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w in Ophrah|strong="H6084"\w*, \w his hometown|strong="H5892"\w*. \w But soon all|strong="H3605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w prostituted themselves|strong="H2181"\w* \w by worshiping it|strong="H310"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w*, \w and it became|strong="H1961"\w* \w a snare|strong="H4170"\w* \w to Gideon|strong="H1439"\w* \w and his household|strong="H1004"\w*.
\s1 Forty Years of Peace
