\c 14
\s1 Samson’s Marriage
\p \v 1 \w One day Samson|strong="H8123"\w* \w went down|strong="H3381"\w* \w to Timnah|strong="H8553"\w*, \w where he saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w . . .|strong="H802"\w* \w a young Philistine|strong="H6430"\w* \w woman|strong="H1323"\w* \w . . .|strong="H8553"\w*. \v 2 \w So he returned|strong="H5927"\w* \w and told|strong="H5046"\w* \w his father|strong="H1"\w* \w and mother|strong="H517"\w* \w -|strong="H559"\w* \w -|strong="H802"\w*, “\w I have seen|strong="H7200"\w* \w a daughter|strong="H1323"\w* \w of the Philistines|strong="H6430"\w* \w in Timnah|strong="H8553"\w*. \w Now|strong="H6258"\w* \w get|strong="H3947"\w* \w her|strong="H853"\w* for me \w as a wife|strong="H802"\w*.”
\p \v 3 \w But his father|strong="H1"\w* \w and mother|strong="H517"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Can’t you [find]|strong="H369"\w* \w a young woman|strong="H1323"\w* \w among your relatives|strong="H251"\w* \w or among any|strong="H3605"\w* \w of our people|strong="H5971"\w*? \w -|strong="H802"\w* \w -|strong="H3588"\w* \w Must you|strong="H859"\w* \w go|strong="H1980"\w* \w to the uncircumcised|strong="H6189"\w* \w Philistines|strong="H6430"\w* \w to get|strong="H3947"\w* \w a wife|strong="H802"\w*?”
