\p \v 5 \w Then Samson|strong="H8123"\w* \w went down|strong="H3381"\w* \w to Timnah|strong="H8553"\w* \w with his father|strong="H1"\w* \w and mother|strong="H517"\w* \w and came|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w the vineyards|strong="H3754"\w* \w of Timnah|strong="H8553"\w*. \w Suddenly|strong="H2009"\w* \w a young lion|strong="H3715"\w* \w . . .|strong="H738"\w* \w came roaring|strong="H7580"\w* \w at him|strong="H7122"\w*, \v 6 \w and the Spirit|strong="H7307"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w came powerfully|strong="H6743"\w* \w upon him|strong="H5921"\w*, \w and he tore the lion apart|strong="H8156"\w* \w with his bare|strong="H3972"\w* \w . . .|strong="H369"\w* \w hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w as one would tear|strong="H8156"\w* \w a young goat|strong="H1423"\w*. \w But he did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w tell|strong="H5046"\w* \w his father|strong="H1"\w* \w or mother|strong="H517"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w what|strong="H834"\w* \w he had done|strong="H6213"\w*. \v 7 \w Then [Samson] continued on his way down|strong="H3381"\w* \w and spoke|strong="H1696"\w* \w to the woman|strong="H802"\w*, \w because|strong="H8123"\w* \w she was pleasing|strong="H3474"\w* \w to his eyes|strong="H5869"\w*.
\s1 Samson’s Riddle
\p \v 8 \w When [Samson] returned|strong="H7725"\w* \w later|strong="H3117"\w* \w to take her|strong="H3947"\w*, \w he left|strong="H5493"\w* \w the road to see|strong="H7200"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w the lion’s|strong="H738"\w* \w carcass|strong="H4658"\w*, \w and in [it]|strong="H1472"\w* \w . . .|strong="H738"\w* \w was|strong="H2009"\w* \w a swarm|strong="H5712"\w* \w of bees|strong="H1682"\w*, \w along with their honey|strong="H1706"\w*. \v 9 \w So he scooped|strong="H7287"\w* \w some honey into|strong="H413"\w* \w his hands|strong="H3709"\w* \w and ate it|strong="H398"\w* \w as he went along|strong="H1980"\w* \w . . .|strong="H1980"\w*. \w And when he returned|strong="H1980"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w his father|strong="H1"\w* \w . . .|strong="H413"\w* \w and mother|strong="H517"\w*, \w he gave|strong="H5414"\w* some to them \w and they ate it|strong="H398"\w*. \w But he did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w tell|strong="H5046"\w* them \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w he had taken|strong="H7287"\w* \w the honey|strong="H1706"\w* \w from the lion’s|strong="H738"\w* \w carcass|strong="H1472"\w*.
\p \v 10 \w Then his father|strong="H1"\w* \w went|strong="H3381"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w visit the woman|strong="H802"\w*, \w and Samson|strong="H8123"\w* \w prepared|strong="H6213"\w* \w a feast|strong="H4960"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w*, \w as|strong="H3588"\w* \w . . .|strong="H3651"\w* \w was customary|strong="H6213"\w* \w for the bridegroom|strong="H970"\w*. \v 11 \w And when|strong="H1961"\w* \w [the Philistines] saw him|strong="H7200"\w*,\f + \fr 14:11 \ft Or \fqa when the bride’s parents saw him\ft ; literally \fqa when they saw him\f* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w they selected|strong="H3947"\w* \w thirty|strong="H7970"\w* \w men to accompany him|strong="H4828"\w* \w . . .|strong="H1961"\w* \w . . .|strong="H854"\w*.
