\p “\w Tell us|strong="H2330"\w* \w your riddle|strong="H2420"\w*,” \w they replied|strong="H559"\w*. “\w Let us hear it|strong="H8085"\w*.”
\p \v 14 \w So he said|strong="H559"\w* to them:
\q1 “\w Out of the eater|strong="H398"\w* \w came|strong="H3318"\w* \w something to eat|strong="H3978"\w*,
\q2 \w and out of the strong|strong="H5794"\w* \w came|strong="H3318"\w* \w something sweet|strong="H4966"\w*.”
\p \w For three|strong="H7969"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w they were unable|strong="H3808"\w* \w . . .|strong="H3201"\w* \w to explain|strong="H5046"\w* \w the riddle|strong="H2420"\w*. \v 15 \w So|strong="H1961"\w* \w on the fourth|strong="H7637"\w*\f + \fr 14:15 \ft LXX and Syriac; Hebrew \fqa seventh\f* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w they said|strong="H559"\w* \w to Samson’s|strong="H8123"\w* \w wife|strong="H802"\w*, “\w Entice|strong="H6601"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w your husband|strong="H376"\w* \w to explain|strong="H5046"\w* \w the riddle|strong="H2420"\w* to us, \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w or|strong="H6435"\w* \w we will burn|strong="H8313"\w* \w you|strong="H853"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w and your father’s|strong="H1"\w* \w household|strong="H1004"\w* \w to death|strong="H784"\w*. \w Did you invite us|strong="H7121"\w* here \w . . .|strong="H3808"\w* \w to rob us|strong="H3423"\w*?”
\p \v 16 \w Then Samson’s|strong="H8123"\w* \w wife|strong="H802"\w* \w came to him|strong="H5921"\w*, \w weeping|strong="H1058"\w*, \w and said|strong="H559"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H7535"\w* “\w You hate me|strong="H8130"\w*! \w You do not really|strong="H3808"\w* \w love me|strong="H157"\w*! \w You have posed|strong="H2330"\w* \w to my people|strong="H1121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H5971"\w* . . . \w a riddle|strong="H2420"\w*, \w but have not|strong="H3808"\w* \w explained it to me|strong="H5046"\w*.”
