\p \v 10 \w So the congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w 12,000 {}|strong="H8147"\w* \w . . .|strong="H6240"\w* \w . . .|strong="H505"\w* \w of|strong="H1121"\w* \w their most valiant|strong="H2428"\w* \w men|strong="H376"\w* \w -|strong="H8033"\w* \w and commanded them|strong="H6680"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w -|strong="H559"\w*: “\w Go|strong="H1980"\w* \w and put|strong="H5221"\w* \w -|strong="H853"\w* \w vvv|strong="H6310"\w* \w to the sword|strong="H2719"\w* \w those living|strong="H3427"\w* \w in Jabesh-gilead|strong="H3003"\w* \w . . .|strong="H1568"\w*, \w including women|strong="H802"\w* \w and children|strong="H2945"\w*. \v 11 \w This|strong="H2088"\w* \w . . .|strong="H1697"\w* \w is what|strong="H834"\w* \w you are to do|strong="H6213"\w*: \w Devote to destruction|strong="H2763"\w*\f + \fr 21:11 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \w every|strong="H3605"\w* \w male|strong="H2145"\w*, \w as well as every|strong="H3605"\w* \w female|strong="H802"\w* \w who has had relations with|strong="H3045"\w* \w . . .|strong="H4904"\w* \w a man|strong="H2145"\w*.”
